-- conversations_index — ConversationsController#index  (GET /conversations)
--
-- CANONICAL HEADER. This text is maintained at
-- reports/diaspora/results3/conversations_index/POLICY_HEADER.txt and MUST be
-- re-applied to the top of this file by every extraction. The declaration IS
-- the safeguard: a policy file that simply stops at a wall is
-- indistinguishable from one that covers everything, so an exclusion may not
-- live only in a report.
--
-- ============================================================================
-- ASSUMPTION BASIS (2026-09-26)
-- ============================================================================
-- This endpoint's completeness claim rests on co-evaluation (DISCIPLINE §16),
-- foreclosure (§16b) and its DECLARED independences. It relies on CONFINEMENT
-- (§16c) for NOTHING.
--
-- The certifying pass runs with confinement OFF — no footprint is measured, no
-- confined pair is inferred, and no `ConfinementAssumption` licence is taken.
-- Under that strictly weaker set, on the 18 633-run corpus:
--
--     coverage_complete=True  tree_complete=True  tree_missing=[]
--     missing_branches=0      tree_nodes=105      demand_sets=83
--     truncated=False         solver_lost=0       unevaluable_exprs=[]
--     total_path_conditions=748 211
--
-- Citation: `_covonly_noconf.json` in this directory, reproduced field for
-- field by `_covonly_noconf_c1.json`. The verdict is invariant under both the
-- C1 loader fix and the withdrawal ledger, because with §16c off the shape
-- computation is skipped entirely.
--
-- WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED. `completion.complete` in `coverage_summary.json` is
-- **False**, and this header does not paper over that. It is False because the
-- 2026-09-19 -> 2026-09-26 assumption gate FAILed 71 INFERRED
-- ConfinementAssumptions, and `completion.py` blocks completion on any
-- inferred pair the gate did not PASS. That flag is left standing. This policy
-- is therefore published as COVERAGE-COMPLETE WITH NO CONFINEMENT LICENCE
-- CLAIMED — not as `complete: true`.
--
-- Because no confinement licence is taken, the correctness of those 71
-- verdicts does not bear on this file. For the record: 55 of the 71 are an
-- artifact of the C1 TRACE-CURRENCY defect (the engine measured §16c
-- footprints in bare target names while the gate's `access_trace` measured
-- full call shapes, so clauses (i)/(ii) — a set difference of shape strings —
-- could not pass), and 16 are currency-independent refutations that stand.
-- Every known and suspected defect in this endpoint's confinement layer is in
-- the LICENSING direction, and this claim takes zero licence.
--
--   full write-up : _C1_CURRENCY_FINDING_20260926.md (this directory)
--   ledger        : _confinement_withdrawn.json + .README.txt (71 pairs,
--                   each flagged `currency_suspect` true/false)
--   defect record : docs/CONFINEMENT_PRECISION_20260913.md §2,
--                   tools/_c1_currency_patch.md (Status corrected 2026-09-26)
--   precedent     : comments_index closed the same way — see its
--                   POLICY_HEADER.txt ASSUMPTION BASIS and
--                   docs/CONFINEMENT_PRECISION_20260913.md §5.2, §6.
--
-- ============================================================================
-- SCOPE (Bali decision, 2026-08-31; DISCIPLINE §15)
-- ============================================================================
-- This endpoint's entrypoint is the POST-AUTH action with a SYMBOLIC
-- principal. The authentication stages (principal SELECT by session/token, and
-- the trackable / lastseenable / rememberable / lockable decisions and writes)
-- run ABOVE the entrypoint and are NOT part of this file.
--
-- THE ENDPOINT'S COMPLETE POLICY IS THIS FILE **UNION** THE SHARED
-- AUTH-BOUNDARY POLICY:
--   reports/diaspora/results3/_auth_boundary/BOUNDARY_POLICY.md
-- Consumers that need the whole request (boundary + action) must take the
-- union; this file alone covers the action only.
--
-- On this controller `authenticate_user!` has no `except:`, so an anonymous
-- request never reaches the action at all.
--
-- NOTE: unresolved symbolic binds kept as placeholders:
--   _SYM_RESULT_ActiveRecord__FinderMethods_devise_user_first_1_person_id
--
-- ============================================================================
-- DEPLOYMENT THE CLAIM IS ABOUT  (docs/RC1_LAZY_FETCH_AS_DECISION_20260925.md
-- §6.3; obligation raised there, applied here 2026-09-26)
-- ============================================================================
-- `Rails.env.include?("mod")` (profile.rb:8) is deliberately NOT symbolised:
-- symbolising it would union two deployments into one policy — a weaker and
-- genuinely different claim ("in SOME deployment this row may be read wide") —
-- and would make the lazy column SET itself symbolic, which is incoherent.
--
-- SO A POLICY FILE UNDER THIS HEADER DESCRIBES ONE DEPLOYMENT, AND WHICH ONE
-- DEPENDS ON THE CORPUS IT WAS EXTRACTED FROM. The two corpora for this
-- endpoint are NOT interchangeable on this point:
--
--   * `_redrive_20260919/conversations_index/` (18 623 dumps, driven
--     2026-09-18 with the CURRENT targets.rb under RAILS_ENV=concolic_mod).
--     A policy from this corpus describes a pod whose `Rails.env` matches
--     "mod" — equivalently, the reference's own configuration — and MAKES NO
--     CLAIM ABOUT A NON-MOD POD. `profiles` reads are the narrow Q1 plus a
--     conditionally-gated Q2.
--
--   * `results3/conversations_index/` (18 633 dumps, driven 2026-08-31 with
--     targets.rb.pre_rc1_20260919, under the then-default RAILS_ENV=concolic).
--     This corpus PREDATES the mod fix: every `profiles` read is wide
--     (`SELECT "profiles".*`, 18 columns), because without the `default_scope`
--     `default_projection` reads an empty `select_values` and no lazy reader
--     is installed. A policy from this corpus therefore describes a NON-MOD
--     pod, and must not be read as describing the reference's deployment.
--
-- The COMPLETENESS claim in the ASSUMPTION BASIS above is certified on the
-- second (main) corpus. It transfers to the first because `_verify_corpus.py`
-- certified "VERDICT: BRANCHING IDENTICAL" across all ten request variants
-- (per-seed PC mismatches 0/N, seed multisets identical, error profiles
-- identical) — the RC-1 redrive changed what the mocks RECORD, not which
-- branches the app takes. Completeness transfers; the `profiles` PROJECTION
-- does not, and that is the whole point of this section.
--
-- Env-name safety (re-derived in RC1_LAZY_FETCH_AS_DECISION_20260925.md §6.3,
-- originally `_RAILS_ENV_MOD_FIX_20260919.md` §3): "concolic_mod" trips no
-- other `Rails.env` check in the app — the only name-sensitive checks are
-- `include? "checked"`, `.test?`, `== "production"`,
-- `.start_with?("production")` and `.development?`.
--
-- ============================================================================
-- COMPLETENESS OF THIS POLICY, AND WHERE IT STOPS
-- ============================================================================
-- This file describes the endpoint's data access on every path a real request
-- in this environment can take. Three limits are DECLARED rather than left
-- implicit (REPORT.md §4 carries the full reasoning and evidence):
--
-- 1. PER-ROW ONE-REPRESENTATIVE UNDER-COUNT. A shape issued once per listed
--    row is issued once per REPRESENTATIVE under the sampled-content model
--    (the shared runtime's designed limit; this policy is a SET of shapes, and
--    presence is unaffected). Example: `Conversation#last_author` is
--    `Person.includes(:profile).find_by(id: <row>.author_id)`, so its
--    `:profile` preload (`SELECT profiles.* … person_id = ?`, no LIMIT) fires
--    once per row — real x11 on a 12-conversation request, x1 in the corpus.
--    The MULTIPLICITY of such a shape scales with row count and is excluded
--    from both the under- and the over-emission verdicts (A7-7). THE SHAPES
--    THEMSELVES ARE PRESENT BELOW; only their counts are not asserted.
--
-- 2. ONE DECLARED RENDERER RE-READ. On the `.js` 500 path (index.haml:32
--    NameError) the exception renderer re-inspects the unloaded @visibilities
--    relation and re-issues its paginated read (x4 measured in the real run,
--    x1 in the corpus). That multiplicity belongs to the exception machinery,
--    not to the application; declared in `completion_config.json`
--    (`multiset_renderer_re_reads`) with its reason.
--
-- 3. `_rows_beyond` H4 DECLARATION. The page BEYOND the last page has 0 rows
--    by definition, so will_paginate's `size > 0` conjunct
--    (active_record.rb:70) has one realizable outcome. The True side is not
--    unexplored — it is impossible. The paginated list's own length variable
--    carries 0/1/many in both polarities. Declared in
--    `completion_config.json` (`h4_by_construction`).
--
-- None of these is a path whose SQL is missing from this file. They are limits
-- on asserted MULTIPLICITY (1, 2) and on one branch's REALIZABILITY (3),
-- recorded here so a consumer knows the boundary of what is claimed.
-- ============================================================================

